From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] label S9+ max backlight metadata for M4 SDHMS

# Reason: Fresh boot after0214 confirms brightness is correctly labeled, but SDHMS still logs `10-28 19:23:37.606 ... /sys/class/backlight/panel/max_brightness: fstat failed: EACCES`. A temporary exact label on only max_brightness using the existing type produced no new fstat errors during the 20-second sample; its original `sysfs` label was restored.
# Affected: the existing M4 thermal helper and lock. Extend exact CIL mapping/verification to the adjacent max_brightness node; no new allow, DAC change, threshold, kernel, blob or radio change.
# Verify: helper idempotence/duplicate/conflict/missing-permission fixtures; the temporary runtime relabel test; require both exact rules in the final vendor ext4 image and recheck Enforcing SDHMS logs after fresh boot.
# Rollback: reverse0215, remove its series/lock entries, and rebuild the next M4 package; prior attempt0214 remains preserved.

